{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1435 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ec15a896a60df907d1b4cef41d16908702d839e34deef09f9dcb6d145538b9b6" :edb/db-before-t 1434 :edb/db-after-t 1435 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534747 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:46:38.528Z" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105384 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  Find the image of the triangle shown below under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/853fd7d5c09944a5bacd0c2b3453504f3fa1eea9d8d3b2c3bdd4f0f44889dc16.png)" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105384 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n  Find the image of the triangle shown below under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/853fd7d5c09944a5bacd0c2b3453504f3fa1eea9d8d3b2c3bdd4f0f44889dc16.png)" 13194139534747 false] [17592186105384 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105384 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6), (1,-2),$ and $(-2,4).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/3fd1073b2eaa5aa9c21e537fcc4dc6cf538ab2992c0732f64da50dbcb63d8fd4.png)" 13194139534747 false] [17592186105385 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105385 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/89efcd0ecb51dac08a1102c5a347eea3459f7209de7cbac0a88b192259ca3b7e.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" 13194139534747 false] [17592186105818 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307355 13194139534747 true] [17592186105818 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307369 13194139534747 true] [17592186105818 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307376 13194139534747 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307348 13194139534747 true] [17592186105819 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307383 13194139534747 true] [17592186105820 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307362 13194139534747 true] [17592186105992 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105992 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 false] [17592186105993 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534747 true] [17592186105993 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186105993 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1351/Source/Images/q-162150.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T$?" 13194139534747 false] [17592186105993 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin." 13194139534747 true] [17592186106081 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186106081 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 false] [17592186106081 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" 13194139534747 true] [17592186106081 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" 13194139534747 false] [17592186284138 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/cfcbd4b374456b4a5913289592d875a42caf81fd02984180e68e34c5b82ef905.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186284138 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/cfcbd4b374456b4a5913289592d875a42caf81fd02984180e68e34c5b82ef905.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 false] [17592186284152 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/6501b1a7e9429c786905c11835410111c32ac0337f1ba63bff130d327350316c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186284152 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/6501b1a7e9429c786905c11835410111c32ac0337f1ba63bff130d327350316c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 false] [17592186284152 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(6,3)$, $(8,4)$ and $(10,5).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/a91af151d3dc0e48aef0eef58012f6c9f72aaff02aafae2d55fe0714c29c96e3.png)" 13194139534747 true] [17592186284152 1145 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(6,3)$, $(8,4)$ and $(10,5).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/a91af151d3dc0e48aef0eef58012f6c9f72aaff02aafae2d55fe0714c29c96e3.png)" 13194139534747 false] [17592186289303 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/8978d3bb02b4032b6e3a8b4a85878db647eb8323ac5b0423b5a9a6fab121c7e7.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186289303 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14009909/assets/8978d3bb02b4032b6e3a8b4a85878db647eb8323ac5b0423b5a9a6fab121c7