vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 12 & 2 & -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,12)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(7,-14).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I  only.\"" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307357 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307358 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307359 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307360 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307361 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1041 "selection" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307359 13194139534747 true] [17592186307356 1110 #uuid "12f3fe25-accc-5a2c-a20c-33ff19f5e3d9" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307357 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307357 1111 #uuid "8ea07bb8-28a5-5b21-8daa-e4cc34c8a4dc" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307358 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307358 1111 #uuid "0283521f-3bd0-5b10-a724-d44a0f5ec938" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307359 1034 "I only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307359 1111 #uuid "d9f1cf54-d8b8-5ab6-bddb-4f7dc088114a" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307360 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307360 1111 #uuid "81a68a26-c735-5b55-96f9-76c53053ec22" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307361 1034 "II only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307361 1111 #uuid "d3389f61-d2a1-5488-9abe-13c48c5f0b1d" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307363 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1089 "q-162207" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/57948af956c9b83ed944fafc26e81a5c003401f753bc520e088ffdbd71915c3a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1113 #uuid "875bea68-bfbb-5cce-a8c9-893099395a11" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307362 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a nonsingular matrix. Therefore, the image of our object under the action of  $T$ is a triangle." 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307364 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307365 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307366 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307367 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307368 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1041 "selection" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307366 13194139534747 true] [17592186307363 1110 #uuid "e1e5efe6-9352-5709-abbe-02926409ce77" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307364 1034 "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307364 1111 #uuid "e1baa123-433a-5455-93e2-a61e991b8bea" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307365 1034 "A rectangle" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307365 1111 #uuid "1e910840-1c7f-5a28-8855-dcae3fa3112e" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307366 1034 "A triangle" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307366 1111 #uuid "90d87b2d-3e8d-5184-af36-2ba2ebae24d8" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307367 1034 "A line segment" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307367 1111 #uuid "046bba86-0abd-56c8-98ef-335f9918f806" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307368 1034 "A point, different from the origin" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307368 1111 #uuid "c80c2eef-c71b-516a-98ae-4c7e262a15bf" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307370 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1089 "q-21068" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1100 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,2)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(-1,0)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(16,8)$\n- $(8,2)$\n- $(-4,4)$" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1113 #uuid "ea75fda7-a514-5ed4-bcda-72806b8641ea" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307369 1145 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$ \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(16,8)$, $(8,4)$ and $(-4,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307371 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307372 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307373 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307374 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307375 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1041 "selection" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307372 13194139534747 true] [17592186307370 1110 #uuid "bfec58de-eab4-58db-9cfa-0469208367f1" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307371 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534747 true] [17592186307371 1111 #uuid "e573bd12-c69d-585f-b2f1-b7cc58615357" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307372 1034 "I only" 13194139534747 true] [17592186307372 1103